Hi,

thanks for the answer. Of course, I agree that it makes sense to retrieve
haplogroups with a multivariate analysis on mtDNA sequences. My main point
is about the aim for which the method is used. With "artefactual"
populations I meant that those are not biological populations but
phylogentic ones, which means that the method is correctly interpreting the
data according to the way it is provided. If my aim was to use mtDNA to
infer population structure (since I am forced to use this locus, yeah it's
not a very good excuse, but that's the way it is) with a method like DAPC, I
guess the only thing that I can do is to use a matrix of haplogroup
frequencies for populations and hope the reviewers won't have anything too
bad against that (strictly speaking). In any case, I wouldn't merge a
multilocus autosomal dataset with a one of mtDNA for individuals.

I hope you will agree with that or I will have to throw away the paper I'm
working on (I don't mean to make you feel responsible, of course).

Best

Valeria

